        <h2>What is ErrNotes?</h2>
        <p>ErrNotes (errsolved.com) is a technical blog dedicated to recording and resolving errors encountered during real development work.</p>
        <p>We specialize in error resolution for tools commonly used in development: Docker, Linux, Git, GitHub Actions, Cloudflare, nginx, Node.js, and more. Articles are published in both Japanese and English.</p>

        <h2>Why This Site Exists</h2>
        <p>It started from a simple realization: I kept running into the same errors over and over. Instead of searching from scratch every time, I started writing down how I solved them. What began as personal notes turned into a public site, with the hope that others hitting the same walls might find it useful.</p>

        <h2>About the Author</h2>
        <p>Independently operated. Follow on Bluesky: <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/sasukkun.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@sasukkun.bsky.social</a></p>

        <h2>Content Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>Articles are written with accuracy in mind, but results may vary depending on your environment and software versions. Use the information at your own risk.</p>

